  "slug": "multi-company-tally-review-checklist",
  "title": "Avoiding Company Mix-Ups When Reviewing Multiple Tally Books",
  "description": "Use a short routine to keep exports and voucher comparisons separate when several companies are available.",
  "category": "Accountant and team workflows",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Keep a company reference for each review",
      "body": "List the exact company name and one recognizable voucher or party for that review. Use this list when switching companies in Syncora or TallyPrime. Two companies can use an identical voucher number in the same month."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Reset and recheck filters after switching",
      "body": "Before opening a ledger or day book in the next company, check the selected company and financial year. Confirm the date range and transaction type independently. A filter that fits one review period may not fit another."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Keep reports separated by company",
      "body": "Put the company name and period in the filename of each exported report and confirm the header inside the file. Store or share it only with the intended team. If you find a company mix-up later, regenerate the correct export and identify which earlier file should be disregarded."
    }
  ],
